    "reason": "ROAS was 1.8 (revenue $2,700 on $1,500 spend, CPA $25, AOV $45), less than half of example-a at the same CPA and spend. Whether 1.8 is profitable depends on your margin, which I don't have, so this is a cautious trim rather than a cut. It spends only $50 per day, so an $80 cap should not bind and carries little delivery risk. It does limit overspend if delivery picks up. The 20% reduction is small enough to avoid disrupting learning. If 1.8 is below your breakeven ROAS, pause or restructure the campaign instead. If it is above breakeven, keep it at $80 and re-check after fresh data covering Oct 1-2."
